{# The class string of a text field, emitted and nothing else.

   It lived in `_contact_form` and was copied four times into the
   assistant. The focus ring, the hairline and the error state are one
   rule, so they hang on one place – the same reason `_button_class`
   exists.

   The browser focus ring is kept on top of the accent border rather than
   replacing it: a one pixel border change would make these the only
   fields on the site where keyboard focus is weaker than the default.

   Emits no markup. Pull it with include(), hand it to `class`.
   Params: invalid (bool, optional), spaced (bool, default true – false for
   a field that sits in a row rather than under its label). #}
{#- `default` would swallow an explicit false, so the test is on defined. -#}
{%- set base = ((spaced is defined ? spaced : true) ? 'mt-2 ' : '') ~ 'w-full rounded-lg border bg-white px-4 py-3 text-base text-neutral-900 shadow-sm transition-colors placeholder:text-neutral-500 focus:outline-2 focus:outline-offset-2 focus:outline-accent' -%}
{%- set state = invalid|default(false)
    ? 'border-error-border focus:border-error-border'
    : 'border-neutral-200 focus:border-accent' -%}
{{- base ~ ' ' ~ state -}}
